WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:20.660
*Soft Jazz Music*

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.740
[Man narrating] "I've never been much for smoking"

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.480
"but taking a bullet to the chest will make you a lot less worried"

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.900
"about the slow deaths of the world."

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.620
"Long story short: I took a job I shouldn't have."

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.560
"They say the pretty ones will always get you killed,"

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.000
"but he was so damn handsome, I just couldn't resist."

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:45.460
"I was a frog in a slow pot of boiling water, or the first clown to get into the clown car."

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.520
"You don't know to get out until it's too late."

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:54.000
"One thing led to another and I found myself slow dancing with the devil in the moonlight.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:00.760
"Except instead of leaving room for Jesus, he left room for a 357 Magnum."

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.480
"I won't bore you with the details."

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.140
"So I'll cut right to the quick: a lot of people died because of this man."

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:07.820
*clink*

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:08.440
"Mhrr.."

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.820
"William J..."

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.020
"Dammit. Come on!"
*clink*

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.860
"William J. Barnum a.k.a. The Colonel."

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:23.240
"Just like the clown in my bat mitzvah, I knew he was trouble from the moment I laid eyes on him."

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:28.740
"And just like Bozo, The Magnificent, a lot of people died when he walked into my life."

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.920
*Echos of the Bozo laughing*

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.860
I've been chasing him down ever since. We were like two naked men running on the same treadmill."

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.460
"Uncomfortably close, but always just a step behind."

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.460
"But no one can run forever."
*taps of chalk on blackboard*

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.200
"Especially not with 200 pounds of sweaty detective breathing down your neck."

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.020
"It hasn't been easy though."

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.880
"I can't count how many countries I've cornered him in."

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.080
"Couldn't tell you how many times I've had him in my big, strong hands."
*detective grunting on stuck drawer*

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:01.020
"Every time I think I've got him for good, he somehow manages to slip away."

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.060
"But he's running out of holes to hide in."

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.860
"I mean that literally, metaphorically, and euphemistically."

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.960
"It doesn't matter how crafty you think you are..."

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.740
Abe: Mmm.. Mhm..*laughs*
"If you've been on the run for years and years..."

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.900
Abe: Alright, perfect! ..Thanks.
"Eventually..."

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.780
"...you're gonna make a mistake."

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:24.200
"Word of advice: if you're running away from your problems, never become too attached to anything."

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.620
"Family, lovers,.."

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.220
"..briefcases on top of your car..."

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.140
*Thumps of briefcase*

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.340
"Some things are best left behind."

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:40.040
"The Colonel's a slippery one, shedding names as easily as a snake sheds a few pounds before bikini season."

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.020
"He's gone through pseudonym after pseudonym trying to cover his tracks."

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.820
"But he always manages to fall back into the same familiar roles..."

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.260
"Drinking, fighting,..."

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.160
"...flirting,..."

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.820
"...dancing."

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.880
*Jazz Music fades into faster Disco Music*

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:20.980
*Disco Music*

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:27.800
"The Colonel was always one for the eccentrics, but his latest persona takes the entire cake shop."

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.440
"Wilford."

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:30.640
" 'Motherloving'."

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.080
"Warfstache."

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:59.260
*Anders Bothén – Boogie Down 5﻿*

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.240
*Gunshots*

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.700
*People screaming over Disco Music*

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.480
*Disco Music fading slightly*

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:34.340
*Anders Bothén – Boogie Down 5﻿ still playing*

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.960
Get your ass down here.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.380
Don't move, asshole!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.300
Show me your hands!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.880
Not like that. Put 'em down!

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.120
*Gunshot*

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:49.460
*Gunshot*

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.460
*Static as Disco Music distorts and dies out *

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.560
Abe: Get down on the ground. Get down on the ground right now!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.660
Wilford: Wh-why'd the music stop?

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.020
Abe: You're not getting away from me this time asshole. I said get your ass down on the ground.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.400
Wilford: Do I know you, friend?

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.260
Abe: I said GET DOWN ON--!

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.220
What?... How do you not--?

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.180
Abe: Stop playing games. Get your ass down on the ground before I blow you right here, RIGHT NOW!

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.540
...away.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.260
Wilford: Dave? Daaaave! Dave?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:24.540
Dave!

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.540
Greg. Steve?

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:31.780
Bill? Dave! I knew I recognized you. How are you? How's the wife?

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.720
Abe: I don't have a wife. STOP stalling!

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.220
You're under arrest for the murder of way too many people to even count!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.460
Wilford: Well, that's just ridiculous! I would never kill anybody.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.000
Abe: Oh, is that right?

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.720
Well, whatever you say, buddy.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.900
*Electric charge from taser gun*

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.780
Wilford: AHHOAhoohaaa...

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.280
*Clicks of a small chain*

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:01.180
*Soft Jazz Music*

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.140
Abe: You ran a real good race there, buddy.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.140
*Abe trying to get engine started*

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.280
Abe: But it's the end of the road for you.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.740
Abe: The law is gonna throw every book they have at you and after that,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.260
they're gonna throw you in a cell and after that,

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.340
they're gonna throw away the key and after that, they're gonna throw that...

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:20.580
cell...

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.300
into a lake.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.012
Abe, (inner monalogue): "But not before I throw a few things at him first."

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.340
"We're gonna play pin the tail on the donkey."

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.500
"But he's the donkey, and the tail, is my feelings."

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.520
"But I shouldn't get ahead of myself."

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.720
"I only get one night with him to fill the hole in my heart he left behind."

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.380
"It's finally time to get some answers."

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.080
Wilford (in Abe's head): "Did we date at some point?"

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.600
Abe: "No! We didn't date. The hole is a metaphor for when you shot me in the --"

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.420
Wilford: Car...

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.160
*Abe screams as a car horn sounds, tires squealing*

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.940
Abe (in thoughts): "Holy shit that was close!"

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.620
Wilford: "We could have taken them."

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.440
Abe: "What the hell does that have to do with-?"

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.540
Abe: How did you...? How ARE YOU --?!

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.940
(Abe, in his thoughts): "How many fingers am I holding up?"

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.120
Wilford: Four..?

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:17.720
Abe: "Aardvark!"

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.320
"Pumpernickel!"

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.160
Wilford: What are you doing?
Abe: "Calabasas!"

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.640
Wilford: "Are you oookaaaayy?"

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.660
Abe: HOW ARE YOU IN MY HEAD?!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.020
Wilford: Why are you shouting?!

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:27.480
Abe: "GET OUT OF MY HEAD!"

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.840
Wilford: "YOU'RE STILL SHOUTING!"

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.660
*both screaming* AAAAHHHH

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.300
*electric charge of taser gun over their yelling*

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.720
Wilford: HnaAAaohh AAaAHh OoOOaH Ooahf nha-ah.. Ooah.. aah?

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.200
Abe: Enough games!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:47.240
Your ass, is mine for the next 24 hours.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.860
Abe: And I'm gonna take my sweet time...

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.860
...with that ass.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.540
Abe: To get, answers out of it...

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.040
from you.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:06.140
Wilford: W-well, I- I suppose I could stay here a while, get comfortable...*sigh*

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.780
Lovely place you've got here!

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:09.320
Could use a bit more color...

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.320
Abe: Enough!! With your bullshit!

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.580
Do you have any remorse?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:19.720
Any remorse at all for the things you've done or are you too much of a coward to face your crimes?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.960
Wilford: Well, there's no need for name-calling!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:27.080
Words can hurt you know, you should be kind and courteous!

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.080
Abe: Name-calling, huh? *chuckle*

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.500
And, uh, what name, would you prefer, huh?

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:34.480
*clank*

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.660
*clank*bu-ftf*tssff*

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:38.100
*clank*clonk*

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.520
Abe: Is it...

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.120
William J. Butterfield?

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.920
Wilford (chuckling): Well- well now, that's a name I- oowww

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:51.000
Abe: Wilson Jackson Bartholomew the III?

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.800
Wilford: Well now I actually married into thaaa-at.. name...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.280
Abe: Wingleheimer!

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.280
(softer) Wait, just... Wingleheimer?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.120
Wilford: Alright, I may have been having a little bit of fun with that one- Oo-OW.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.860
Abe: NAME, AFTER NAME, AFTER name after name!

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:11.520
Just, so you can distance yourself from the real name you should be called.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.800
(softly) Murderer.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:21.300
Wilford: (softly) Abe?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:26.540
Abe! Abe, it's been years!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.640
How are you? How are you doing? How's the family?

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.940
Abe: Oh, I'm doing just peachy, Buddy!

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.800
'cause I've been waiting a long, long time for this day to come,

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.920
so we could sit down, have a chat.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.040
Catch up; good and proper.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:44.680
Wilford: Wow...

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.020
There we all are!

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.560
Abe: How the hell did you do that?!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.260
Wilford: We look so young!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.360
Abe: You better get your ass BACK in that chair!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.040
Also, how did you get your ass out of that chair?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.180
You're gonna tell me, you're gonna tell me, how you got your ass out of that chair

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.660
so I can figure out a way to get it back IN that chair!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.940
Wilford: Oh there's Celine... my heart still beats for her to this day!

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:08.780
But if she- saw me she'd probably carve mine out! *laughs*

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:09.540
Abe: What?

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:11.540
Wilford: (softly) How did you find all this?

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:15.260
Abe: I've-I've-I've... I've always had them! I've been collecting them.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:19.380
Every single scrap of evidence this whole time so that one day,

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:19.880
*cocks gun*

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.400
I can bring you down.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.880
Wilford: (softly) That's so sweet.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.560
Abe: It's not sweet, that's sickening!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:25.900
Wilford: Sickeningly sweeeet!

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.320
Abe: That's not what I meant!

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:31.260
Wilford: Look I am terribly, terribly, sorry that I didn't remember you.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.800
Memories start to get jumbled after a while.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.820
(softly) Sometimes I, forget even the simplest of things...

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:41.880
Abe: Oh, trust me. You'll have plenty of time to think about all the horrible things

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:46.520
you've done once they throw you in a cage, then throw away the key, and then throw that-

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:50.520
HOW THE HELL YOU KEEP DOING THAT?!

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:56.820
Wilford: Things get jumbled so easily! The when, the where, the why, the how of it all - and who can keep track of it?

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:59.460
I wonder what he's up to, have you seen him?

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.720
(softly) ...maybe I should stop by.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.460
Abe: You seriously need to get back in the chair.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:07.220
I- I- I- I- I've got more rope. Maybe that'll work.

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.920
Wilford: Eh, worth a shot.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:10.300
Oh!

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:16.480
The train! Oh, I remember the train! How long were we stuck in the snow for?

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:17.920
Abe: What?

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:19.280
Wilford: Oh, you don't remember?

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.300
Ah, that's okay. Probably hasn't happened yet,

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.480
ohhh, but some of your finest work, I have to say.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:28.060
A little spoiler alert for later to make it easier on you.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.540
(whispering) We all did it. *chuckles*

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:31.080
Abe: I don't underST-Aa --!

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:31.580
*gunshot*

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.760
Wilford: Shush, shush, shush, shush, shush.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.500
*kisses the barrel* Not now.

00:11:35.509 --> 00:11:37.509
The grown-ups are talking.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.040
Save that for later.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.140
Abe: (quietly) What the hell's going on?

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:41.800
Wilford: Huh?

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:49.200
I don't really know. Honestly, I- I- I don't understand anything anymore... but I do remember you.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:54.400
And I remembered that there's something I've been meaning to give you

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.460
after ALL - THESE - YEARS!

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.860
*Suspense music builds up*

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.060
*squeaky toy noise*

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.000
I'm sorry.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:03.860
Abe: GET OFF o- MmM...eee..

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:10.280
Wilford: If there's one thing I've learned after all these years it's that nothing heals like a good apology!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.740
Abe: I don't... understand anything anymore...

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:14.860
Wilford: Exactly!

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.740
None of this makes any sense! That's the beauty of it!

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:20.840
Abe: Beauty...?

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:25.540
What about any of this, is beautiful to you?!

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:30.660
What kind of- sick, twisted, SON OF A BITCH,

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.240
THINKS ANY OF THIS, IS BEAUTIFUL?!

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.580
Wilford: Now what did we say about name-calling?

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:38.500
Abe: YOOOUU KILLED PEOPLE!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.540
SO MANY PEOPLE!

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:44.400
(verge of tears) You killed my friends! You killed my partner!

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.760
You shot... ME!

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.960
Wilford: Now, it SEEMS to me like you're trying to paint me as the bad guy.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.760
Abe: (screaming) YOU ARE THE BAD GUY!!!

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:53.400
Wilford: (calmly) Okay, whoa!

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.820
Hey, whoa, time out. Time out. Time out.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:59.220
Shhh... Uh, woah, hey! Hoo-hah hee-hey. Time out!

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.120
I get it, you've been hunting me...

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.900
For years, and years, and years. You've been chasing me, all around the world.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:10.740
Uh... from bedrooms, to bathrooms, to ballrooms.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:14.580
You've been chasing me and you've been doing a real bang-up job of it,

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.940
But, an- and forgive me, if this sounds ins- ULting in any way,

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:26.280
What would you say, our- Uh, o- our closest encounter was, before this VERY moment right here?

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.020
Abe: When was our closest encounter?

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:29.820
Wilford: Yuh-yeah.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:30.880
Abe: Before this very moment?

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:31.560
Wilford: Yes.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.300
Abe: That's easy.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:34.640
It was when we...

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.340
*Abe falters*

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:36.960
When...

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.340
We, uh...

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.080
You...

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:44.920
Ye-Yeah ah, it was when you, um...

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:46.600
That's when you, um... *clears throat*

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.180
I was hunting you down, I was stalking you,

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.360
but you fled the country, to - uh...

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:55.920
Um...

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:00.860
All right, all right, yeah ye- ye- yeah, you were, you were off the radar for three years,

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.120
BUT! I got a hot tip that you had shacked up in...

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:06.300
Uh... in, um - ah...

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.140
You shacked up with...

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.420
In, uh... uh... with the...

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.900
Wilford: Three years... uh, what year was that, exactly?

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.600
Abe: What, what year?

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:19.860
Wilford (softly): Yes.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.900
Abe: Well, u-uh, it was in, uh, i- it was in, um...

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:27.900
*Abe falters again*

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.640
It... was uh...

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.120
It was - um...

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:36.920
(softly) I...

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.340
I can't re-member...

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.460
I...

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:46.120
I've - uh...

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.180
*sighs*

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.240
I've obsessed over this case for - uh, years...

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.680
Every, moment of every day....

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:06.180
Spent trying to hunt you down...

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.540
So why can't I remember?

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:16.000
Am I crazy?

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.900
Wilford: No! No-no. No, no, no, no!

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:23.760
My friend, you are NOT, crazy.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:27.680
Don't let ANYone, EVer, tell you that you're, crazy.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:31.500
Y-you're just too focused on the minutiae of it--

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.240
The details, the who killed who, the who slept with who.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:37.320
It- you're not focusing on the big picture.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:41.960
Abe: It's impossible, to know things that haven't happened yet.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.160
Wilford: Yes, exactly!

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:52.120
Just, like it's impossible - to survive a bullet - (softly) through the heart.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:54.640
*faint echoing gunshot*

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:59.980
*piano song from the final scene of Who Killed Markiplier starts playing*

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.540
Abe, (inner monalogue): "This was all a nightmare that I couldn't wake up from."

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:06.800
"My heart was pounding Morse code in my ears, but I never learned the language."

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.800
"My mind was like a hamster ball rolling down the freeway -"

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.840
"no matter how fast I went I couldn't keep up with the flow."

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.900
"It was my first year of Clown College all over again and I--.."

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:18.900
Wilford: No, no, nope, nope, nope, no... no.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.960
No drifting off just yet.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.120
Listen, friend.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:26.220
It was a bit of a shock for me, too.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.260
Life needed a bit of madness, but...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.760
(softly) why should death be any different?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:37.400
But I think the stress, is getting to you a little bit. You need to unwind.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:42.780
You're- you're a freshly born fawn, trying to find your legs in the world that doesn't make sense.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:45.000
So, just for tonight...

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:51.640
Let's forget about all the- th- the chasing and, the killing and, the shooty shooty bang bang, "God, you're a murderer!"

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:52.800
*chuckles*

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.100
And just for tonight...(light static)

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.880
Why don't we...

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:00.000
have a little fun?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
*piano continues playing*

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:24.560
*Disco music plays *

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.600
*ding*

